11... { -KEY- } Ra3 { The rest is easy. } 12. Ke2 Kf6 13. Kd2 Ke6 14. Kc2 f6 15. Kb2 Ra4 16. Kb3 Ra1 17. Kb4 Kd6 18. Rh7 $1 { By their previous move Black managed to prevent the enemy king from moving further towards the a-pawn, but now they can't hold the kingside at the same time. } ( { In effect, } 18. Kb5 $6 Rb1 { wouldn't make sense for White now that Black's king is covering the c6 and c7-squares. } ) 
